# 🚀 API & Integration Documentation (Frontend-to-Backend Contract)

## 1. Authentication Module 🔐

### A. Citizen Registration

* **Endpoint:** `POST /api/auth/register`
* **Description:** Registers a new citizen user. Geo-fenced data is strictly validated.
* **Content-Type:** `application/json`
* **Request Body:**
```json
{
  "name": "Hamza Meer",
  "mobile": "9876543210",
  "email": "meer@example.com",
  "address": "Zone 1, MP Nagar",
  "state": "Madhya Pradesh",
  "city": "Bhopal",
  "pincode": "462001",
  "password": "hashed_password"
}

```


* **Expected Response (201 Created):** `{ "message": "Citizen registered successfully", "userId": "..." }`

### B. Universal Login

* **Endpoint:** `POST /api/auth/login`
* **Description:** Unified login for all 4 roles. Issues a session/JWT token.
* **Content-Type:** `application/json`
* **Request Body:**
```json
{
  "role": "Citizen | Supervisor | DeptHead | SuperAdmin",
  "username": "meer@example.com", 
  "password": "password123"
}

```


* **Expected Response (200 OK):** `{ "message": "Login successful", "role": "Citizen", "token": "..." }`

